From c25fc64b6faa17ed25858b2f49a55432352f36dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:26:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(trace): decline a failed startup definition that
 reads DOMAIN of a function TLC keeps lazy

TLC keeps a function constructor lazy where its domain isn't a set
enumeration or an interval, and its DOMAIN gives that domain as TLC
holds it, as SUBSET S a SubsetValue. The evaluator builds the function
and its domain eagerly, so an operation on the domain can fail before
TLC fails elsewhere: {DOMAIN [b \in SUBSET {1} |-> 1] \ (3 .. 3),
CHOOSE y \in {} : TRUE} fails at the CHOOSE in TLC and in the
difference in the evaluator, a wrong output since the startup guards.
Such a failure now declines, but where Cardinality counts the domain,
which TLC sizes as the evaluator does.
